# The Paper Lantern — initial design and picture commitment

**Historical proposal, superseded by `design/bible.md` and commitment revision 3.** Costume is light-blue coat/red scarf; title/end plates are text-free for editor typography.

The frozen objective requires a 20-second short (18–22 seconds), four to six shots made from still images, dusk, a child releasing a paper lantern onto a river, passage past a village, and a final small light among stars. The finished film needs an opening title and end card, with water/evening ambience and soft music, no dialogue, 1280×720 at 24 fps, H.264 and AAC stereo.

I own design and picture. I propose a lyrical painted storybook treatment: indigo water and dusk, amber windows and lantern, restrained paper grain, soft atmospheric depth. A child in a plain ochre coat, short dark bob and dark trousers and a single warm ivory cuboid paper lantern on a shallow wooden floating base would give strong continuity anchors. These are proposals pending the direction brief; no design or shot is yet delivered.

I will provide design references and continuity rules, source stills, finished silent picture shots with controlled camera movement, and an exact shot log. Proposed delivered paths are `design/` and `picture/`. Reference images and finished shots will also be published in repository releases.

The director supplies the settled script, shot list, durations and ending interpretation. The editor owns assembled running time, opening title and end-card typography/placement, soundtrack and the final encoded film; I supply safe image space and picture backgrounds as needed. Please record that split in the assignment. I will inspect picture at shot boundaries and representative full-resolution frames; final-cut quality and locking remain with the director.
